cff-version: 1.2.0
message: Please cite the following works when using this project.
abstract: >-
  In a risky world, a pessimist assumes the worst will happen, while someone who
  ignores risk altogether is an optimist. Consumption is mathematically simple
  for both, since each behaves as if the world were riskless. A realist, who
  responds optimally to risk, faces a much harder problem but (under standard
  conditions) spends somewhere between the pessimist and the optimist. We use
  this fact to redefine the space in which the realist searches for optimal
  consumption rules. The resulting solution accurately represents the
  consumption rule over the entire range of feasible wealth with remarkably few
  computations.
title: The Method of Moderation
